; A value expression is parsed when the option is given, so the commodity
; styles its text teaches are in place before a later --decimal-comma: here
; "25,500 EUR" read before --decimal-comma gives EUR a thousands mark, which
; the display keeps.  The base parsed the expression after every option and
; printed 51000,000 EUR in either order.

2015/01/01 Buy stocks
    Assets:Investments         2000 FOO @@ 20,00 EUR
    Assets:Cash                           -20,00 EUR

test bal assets:investments -V --value-expr "25,500 EUR" --decimal-comma
      51.000,000 EUR  Assets:Investments
end test

test bal assets:investments -V --decimal-comma --value-expr "25,500 EUR"
       51000,000 EUR  Assets:Investments
end test
